[h2]Build 0.9.124[/h2]
[h3]Added[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]The industrial repair center can break down[/b], like other powered machines, and is fixed with a component. How often follows its overclock: about a quarter of the usual rate at 10%, the usual rate at 100%, over three times it at 200%. Running it hard now has a real cost.
[*][b]It sounds like the job it is doing.[/b] While working it plays the sound of the item's own crafting: a sewing machine for clothes, the smithy for blades and armor, machining for guns. It also lights up while a job runs.
[*][b]A Status tab.[/b] Shows what it is doing and the time left, what the current overclock costs in power, heat and breakdowns, what is waiting on the item spot - whether it will be repaired, recycled or rejected, and the materials a repair needs against what is on the material spots - and anything waiting for a reject chute.
[*][b]Vanilla Furniture Expanded - Factory:[/b] the repair center now sits in VFE's Factories build tab, with the factory hopper offered alongside it, like VFE's own machines.
[*][b]Vanilla Memes Expanded:[/b] the automation efficiency precepts speed up or slow down its jobs, as they do VFE Factory's machines.
[/list]
[list]
[*]Safe to update mid-save.
[/list]
